==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|en-au-go-getter.ogg|a=AU}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} An {{l|en|active}} and {{l|en|enterprising}} person; one who is [[motivated]] or [[inclined]] to [[excel]]; one who [[strives]] to achieve [[success]] or [[improvement]].
#: {{ux|en|He's a promising young '''go-getter''', but he needs to learn some things about office politics.}}
#: {{ux|en|Tom Pitella is a '''go-getter''' and does not rely on others to prove things in the field of mathematics to him.}}
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=1950|author=Norman Lindsay|authorlink=Norman Lindsay|title={{w|Dust or Polish?}}|publisher=Angus and Robertson|location=Sydney|page=171|passage="Then I hope you've taken its moral lesson to heart." "What's that?" "The awful possibilities of being submerged by the insidious urge of the '''go-getter''', and forgetting about the really important things of life."}}
#* {{quote-book|en |year=2008 |title=Identical |author=Ellen Hopkins |page=31|ISBN=1416984658|passage=I must get it from my dad. Can't be from Mom, the world-class '''go-getter''', hand shaker, and baby kisser.” }}

